.SH "COMMAND DESCRIPTIONS"
.IX Header "COMMAND DESCRIPTIONS"
.SS addgroup
.IX Subsection "addgroup"
addgroup [\-g GID] [\-S] [USER] GROUP
.PP
Add a group or add a user to a group
.PP
.Vb 2
\&        \-g GID  Group id
\&        \-S      Create a system group
.Ve
.SS adduser
.IX Subsection "adduser"
adduser [OPTIONS] USER [GROUP]
.PP
Create new user, or add USER to GROUP
.PP
.Vb 9
\&        \-h DIR          Home directory
\&        \-g GECOS        GECOS field
\&        \-s SHELL        Login shell
\&        \-G GRP          Group
\&        \-S              Create a system user
\&        \-D              Don\*(Aqt assign a password
\&        \-H              Don\*(Aqt create home directory
\&        \-u UID          User id
\&        \-k SKEL         Skeleton directory (/etc/skel)
.Ve
.SS arp
.IX Subsection "arp"
arp 
[\-vn]	[\-H HWTYPE] [\-i IF] \-a [HOSTNAME]
[\-v]		    [\-i IF] \-d HOSTNAME [pub]
[\-v]	[\-H HWTYPE] [\-i IF] \-s HOSTNAME HWADDR [temp]
[\-v]	[\-H HWTYPE] [\-i IF] \-s HOSTNAME HWADDR [netmask MASK] pub
[\-v]	[\-H HWTYPE] [\-i IF] \-Ds HOSTNAME IFACE [netmask MASK] pub
.PP
Manipulate ARP cache
.PP
.Vb 9
\&        \-a              Display (all) hosts
\&        \-d              Delete ARP entry
\&        \-s              Set new entry
\&        \-v              Verbose
\&        \-n              Don\*(Aqt resolve names
\&        \-i IF           Network interface
\&        \-D              Read HWADDR from IFACE
\&        \-A,\-p AF        Protocol family
\&        \-H HWTYPE       Hardware address type
.Ve
.SS ash
.IX Subsection "ash"
ash [\-il] [\-|+Cabefmnuvx] [\-|+o OPT]... [\-c \*(AqSCRIPT\*(Aq [ARG0 ARGS] | FILE ARGS | \-s ARGS]
.PP
Unix shell interpreter
.SS awk
.IX Subsection "awk"
awk [OPTIONS] [AWK_PROGRAM] [FILE]...
.PP
.Vb 4
\&        \-v VAR=VAL      Set variable
\&        \-F SEP          Use SEP as field separator
\&        \-f/\-E FILE      Read program from FILE
\&        \-e AWK_PROGRAM
.Ve
.SS basename
.IX Subsection "basename"
basename FILE [SUFFIX] | \-a FILE... | \-s SUFFIX FILE...
.PP
Strip directory path and SUFFIX from FILE
.PP
.Vb 2
\&        \-a              All arguments are FILEs
\&        \-s SUFFIX       Remove SUFFIX (implies \-a)
.Ve
.SS blkid
.IX Subsection "blkid"
blkid [BLOCKDEV]...
.PP
Print UUIDs of all filesystems
.SS cat
.IX Subsection "cat"
cat [\-nbvteA] [FILE]...
.PP
Print FILEs to stdout
.PP
.Vb 6
\&        \-n      Number output lines
\&        \-b      Number nonempty lines
\&        \-v      Show nonprinting characters as ^x or M\-x
\&        \-t      ...and tabs as ^I
\&        \-e      ...and end lines with $
\&        \-A      Same as \-vte
.Ve
.SS chgrp
.IX Subsection "chgrp"
chgrp [\-RhLHPcvf]... GROUP FILE...
.PP
Change the group membership of FILEs to GROUP
.PP
.Vb 8
\&        \-h      Affect symlinks instead of symlink targets
\&        \-L      Traverse all symlinks to directories
\&        \-H      Traverse symlinks on command line only
\&        \-P      Don\*(Aqt traverse symlinks (default)
\&        \-R      Recurse
\&        \-c      List changed files
\&        \-v      Verbose
\&        \-f      Hide errors
.Ve
.SS chmod
.IX Subsection "chmod"
chmod [\-Rcvf] MODE[,MODE]... FILE...
.PP
MODE is octal number (bit pattern sstrwxrwxrwx) or [ugoa]{+|\-|=}[rwxXst]
.PP
.Vb 4
\&        \-R      Recurse
\&        \-c      List changed files
\&        \-v      Verbose
\&        \-f      Hide errors
.Ve
.SS chown
.IX Subsection "chown"
chown [\-RhLHPcvf]... USER[:[GRP]] FILE...
.PP
Change the owner and/or group of FILEs to USER and/or GRP
.PP
.Vb 8
\&        \-h      Affect symlinks instead of symlink targets
\&        \-L      Traverse all symlinks to directories
\&        \-H      Traverse symlinks on command line only
\&        \-P      Don\*(Aqt traverse symlinks (default)
\&        \-R      Recurse
\&        \-c      List changed files
\&        \-v      Verbose
\&        \-f      Hide errors
.Ve
.SS clear
.IX Subsection "clear"
clear
.PP
Clear screen
.SS comm
.IX Subsection "comm"
comm [\-123] FILE1 FILE2
.PP
Compare FILE1 with FILE2
.PP
.Vb 3
\&        \-1      Suppress lines unique to FILE1
\&        \-2      Suppress lines unique to FILE2
\&        \-3      Suppress lines common to both files
.Ve
.SS cp
.IX Subsection "cp"
cp [\-arPLHpfinlsTu] SOURCE DEST
or: cp [\-arPLHpfinlsu] SOURCE... { \-t DIRECTORY | DIRECTORY }
.PP
Copy SOURCEs to DEST
.PP
.Vb 10
\&        \-a      Same as \-dpR
\&        \-R,\-r   Recurse
\&        \-d,\-P   Preserve symlinks (default if \-R)
\&        \-L      Follow all symlinks
\&        \-H      Follow symlinks on command line
\&        \-p      Preserve file attributes if possible
\&        \-f      Overwrite
\&        \-i      Prompt before overwrite
\&        \-n      Don\*(Aqt overwrite
\&        \-l,\-s   Create (sym)links
\&        \-T      Refuse to copy if DEST is a directory
\&        \-t DIR  Copy all SOURCEs into DIR
\&        \-u      Copy only newer files
.Ve
.SS crc32
.IX Subsection "crc32"
crc32 FILE...
.PP
Calculate CRC32 checksum of FILEs
.SS cttyhack
.IX Subsection "cttyhack"
cttyhack [PROG ARGS]
.PP
Give PROG a controlling tty if possible.
Example for /etc/inittab (for busybox init):
	::respawn:/bin/cttyhack /bin/sh
Giving controlling tty to shell running with PID 1:
	$ exec cttyhack sh
Starting interactive shell from boot shell script:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&        setsid cttyhack sh
.Ve
.SS cut
.IX Subsection "cut"
cut {\-b|c LIST | \-f|F LIST [\-d SEP] [\-s]} [\-D] [\-O SEP] [FILE]...
.PP
Print selected fields from FILEs to stdout
.PP
.Vb 9
\&        \-b LIST Output only bytes from LIST
\&        \-c LIST Output only characters from LIST
\&        \-d SEP  Input field delimiter (default \-f TAB, \-F run of whitespace)
\&        \-f LIST Print only these fields (\-d is single char)
\&        \-F LIST Print only these fields (\-d is regex)
\&        \-s      Drop lines with no delimiter (else print them in full)
\&        \-D      Don\*(Aqt sort ranges; line without delimiters has one field
\&        \-\-output\-delimiter SEP  Output field delimeter
\&        \-n      Ignored
.Ve
.SS date
.IX Subsection "date"
date [OPTIONS] [+FMT] [[\-s] TIME]
.PP
Display time (using +FMT), or set time
.PP
.Vb 8
\&        \-u              Work in UTC (don\*(Aqt convert to local time)
\&        [\-s] TIME       Set time to TIME
\&        \-d TIME         Display TIME, not \*(Aqnow\*(Aq
\&        \-D FMT          FMT (strptime format) for \-s/\-d TIME conversion
\&        \-r FILE         Display last modification time of FILE
\&        \-R              Output RFC\-2822 date
\&        \-I[SPEC]        Output ISO\-8601 date
\&                        SPEC=date (default), hours, minutes, seconds or ns
.Ve
.PP
Recognized TIME formats:
.PP
.Vb 6
\&        @seconds_since_1970
\&        hh:mm[:ss]
\&        [YYYY.]MM.DD\-hh:mm[:ss]
\&        YYYY\-MM\-DD hh:mm[:ss]
\&        [[[[[YY]YY]MM]DD]hh]mm[.ss]
\&        \*(Aqdate TIME\*(Aq form accepts MMDDhhmm[[YY]YY][.ss] instead
.Ve
.SS dd
.IX Subsection "dd"
dd [if=FILE] [of=FILE] [ibs=N obs=N/bs=N] [count=N] [skip=N] [seek=N]
	[conv=notrunc|noerror|sync|fsync]
	[iflag=skip_bytes|count_bytes|fullblock|direct] [oflag=seek_bytes|append|direct]
.PP
Copy a file with converting and formatting
.PP
.Vb 10
\&        if=FILE         Read from FILE instead of stdin
\&        of=FILE         Write to FILE instead of stdout
\&        bs=N            Read and write N bytes at a time
\&        ibs=N           Read N bytes at a time
\&        obs=N           Write N bytes at a time
\&        count=N         Copy only N input blocks
\&        skip=N          Skip N input blocks
\&        seek=N          Skip N output blocks
\&        conv=notrunc    Don\*(Aqt truncate output file
\&        conv=noerror    Continue after read errors
\&        conv=sync       Pad blocks with zeros
\&        conv=fsync      Physically write data out before finishing
\&        conv=swab       Swap every pair of bytes
\&        iflag=skip_bytes        skip=N is in bytes
\&        iflag=count_bytes       count=N is in bytes
\&        oflag=seek_bytes        seek=N is in bytes
\&        iflag=direct    O_DIRECT input
\&        oflag=direct    O_DIRECT output
\&        iflag=fullblock Read full blocks
\&        oflag=append    Open output in append mode
\&        status=noxfer   Suppress rate output
\&        status=none     Suppress all output
.Ve
.PP
N may be suffixed by c (1), w (2), b (512), kB (1000), k (1024), MB, M, GB, G
.SS delgroup
.IX Subsection "delgroup"
delgroup [USER] GROUP
.PP
Delete group GROUP from the system or user USER from group GROUP
.SS deluser
.IX Subsection "deluser"
deluser [\-\-remove\-home] USER
.PP
Delete USER from the system
.SS df
.IX Subsection "df"
df [\-PkmhTai] [\-B SIZE] [\-t TYPE] [FILESYSTEM]...
.PP
Print filesystem usage statistics
.PP
.Vb 9
\&        \-P      POSIX output format
\&        \-k      1024\-byte blocks (default)
\&        \-m      1M\-byte blocks
\&        \-h      Human readable (e.g. 1K 243M 2G)
\&        \-T      Print filesystem type
\&        \-t TYPE Print only mounts of this type
\&        \-a      Show all filesystems
\&        \-i      Inodes
\&        \-B SIZE Blocksize
.Ve
.SS dmesg
.IX Subsection "dmesg"
dmesg [\-cr] [\-n LEVEL] [\-s SIZE]
.PP
Print or control the kernel ring buffer
.PP
.Vb 4
\&        \-c              Clear ring buffer after printing
\&        \-n LEVEL        Set console logging level
\&        \-s SIZE         Buffer size
\&        \-r              Print raw message buffer
.Ve
.SS dos2unix
.IX Subsection "dos2unix"
dos2unix [\-ud] [FILE]
.PP
Convert FILE in\-place from DOS to Unix format.
When no file is given, use stdin/stdout.
.PP
.Vb 2
\&        \-u      dos2unix
\&        \-d      unix2dos
.Ve
.SS du
.IX Subsection "du"
du [\-aHLdclsxhmk] [FILE]...
.PP
Summarize disk space used for FILEs (or directories)
.PP
.Vb 12
\&        \-a      Show file sizes too
\&        \-b      Apparent size (including holes)
\&        \-L      Follow all symlinks
\&        \-H      Follow symlinks on command line
\&        \-d N    Limit output to directories (and files with \-a) of depth < N
\&        \-c      Show grand total
\&        \-l      Count sizes many times if hard linked
\&        \-s      Display only a total for each argument
\&        \-x      Skip directories on different filesystems
\&        \-h      Sizes in human readable format (e.g., 1K 243M 2G)
\&        \-m      Sizes in megabytes
\&        \-k      Sizes in kilobytes (default)
.Ve
.SS echo
.IX Subsection "echo"
echo [\-neE] [ARG]...
.PP
Print ARGs to stdout
.PP
.Vb 3
\&        \-n      No trailing newline
\&        \-e      Interpret backslash escapes (\et=tab etc)
\&        \-E      Don\*(Aqt interpret backslash escapes (default)
.Ve
.SS env
.IX Subsection "env"
env [\-i0] [\-u NAME]... [\-] [NAME=VALUE]... [PROG ARGS]
.PP
Print current environment or run PROG after setting up environment
.PP
.Vb 3
\&        \-, \-i   Start with empty environment
\&        \-0      NUL terminated output
\&        \-u NAME Remove variable from environment
.Ve
.SS fdisk
.IX Subsection "fdisk"
fdisk [\-uls] [\-C CYLINDERS] [\-H HEADS] [\-S SECTORS] [\-b SSZ] [\-t PARTTYPE] DISK
.PP
Change partition table
.PP
.Vb 8
\&        \-u              Start and End are in sectors (instead of cylinders)
\&        \-l              Show partition table for each DISK, then exit
\&        \-s              Show sizes in kb for each DISK, then exit
\&        \-b 2048         (for certain MO disks) use 2048\-byte sectors
\&        \-T PARTTYPE     Force \*(Aqdos\*(Aq partition if \*(Aqgpt\*(Aq also present
